# Walkthrough: Python 3.11 Environment Enforcement

The goal of this task was to stabilize the backend workspace environment by explicitly enforcing a Python 3.11 virtual environment, which is required for critical C-extension ML dependencies.

## Changes Made

### 1. Environment Purge & Rebuild
- The existing `backend/venv` (which was incorrectly running Python 3.14.4) was completely removed.
- A new, clean virtual environment was explicitly created using the local Python 3.11 binary via `py -3.11 -m venv D:\AI ML Project\backend\venv`.
- The IDE configuration in `.vscode/settings.json` was verified and confirmed to already be pointing accurately to the `backend/venv` path.

### 2. Dependency Installation & Locking
- We activated the new 3.11 virtual environment and successfully installed the required pipeline dependencies: `fastapi uvicorn websockets ultralytics mediapipe opencv-python edge-tts langchain-core`.
- The resolved dependency tree was successfully frozen back into `backend/requirements.txt`.

## Diagnostic Verification Report

A diagnostic script was executed within the new virtual environment to verify the active interpreter and dependency integrity. 

> [!WARNING]
> While the environment has been successfully rebuilt on Python 3.11, the diagnostic check uncovered a strict OS-level security policy that is blocking the execution of PyTorch binaries. 

